{"resourceType":"DocumentReference","id":"note-30d61d45-d446-a898-1906-e97ed5fa2119","author":[{"display":"Dr. Casey Morgan","reference":"Practitioner/longwood-endocrine-longwood-endocrine-practitioner"},{"display":"LONGWOOD ENDOCRINE","reference":"Organization/longwood-endocrine"}],"category":[{"coding":[{"code":"clinical-note","display":"Clinical Note","system":"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/CodeSystem/us-core-documentreference-category"}],"text":"Clinical Note"}],"content":[{"attachment":{"contentType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","data":""},"format":{"code":"urn:ihe:iti:xds:2017:mimeTypeSufficient","system":"http://ihe.net/fhir/ihe.formatcode.fhir/CodeSystem/formatcode"}}],"context":{"encounter":[{"reference":"Encounter/30d61d45-d446-a898-1906-e97ed5fa2119"}],"period":{"end":"2026-03-25T16:15:55.000Z","start":"2026-03-25T16:00:55.000Z"}},"date":"2026-03-25T16:00:55.769Z","status":"current","subject":{"reference":"Patient/Alden-Chong-Murphy"},"text":{"status":"generated","div":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><pre>2026-03-25\n\n## Pediatric type 1 diabetes endocrinology follow-up note\n# Narrative\n- Chief Complaint: Diabetes mellitus type 1\n\n# History of Present Illness\n- History: Routine quarterly endocrinology follow-up for established type 1 diabetes. Family reviewed home glucose trends, hypoglycemia frequency, insulin doses, sick-day plan, and growth since the last visit.\n\n# Plan\n- Plan: Continue current insulin modality with dose or automation titration based on glucose trends and HbA1c, reinforce hypoglycemia and sick-day management, and follow up in approximately 3 months alternating with diabetes education.\n- Disposition: Discharged home from clinic with planned routine quarterly diabetes education or endocrinology follow-up.\n\n# Clinical Context\n- Data availability: Most key T1D diagnostic and longitudinal milestones are available as structured local data in this record.\n- Note-only items: No major T1D-specific note-only items are flagged in this record.\n\n# Observations\n- Body height: 156 cm\n- Body weight: 54.2 kg\n- Body mass index (BMI) [Ratio]: 22.29 kg/m2\n- Heart rate: 80 /min\n- Body temperature: 36.7 Cel\n\n# Reports\n- Report: Laboratory report (2026-03-25 16:00)\n- Hemoglobin A1c/Hemoglobin.total in Blood: 7.92067 %\n- Glucose [Mass/volume] in Blood: 195.112 mg/dL\n- Report: Laboratory report (2026-03-25 16:00)\n- Average glucose [Mass/volume] in Interstitial fluid during Reporting Period: 180.623 mg/dL\n\n# Encounter\n- Encounter type: ambulatory\n- Encounter label: T1D endocrinology follow-up\n- Reason: Diabetes mellitus type 1\n\n# Assessment\n- Assessment: Established type 1 diabetes; glycemic control is being reassessed against HbA1c, time-in-range data when available, and reported hypoglycemia.\n- Current regimen: Hybrid closed-loop automated insulin delivery with a compatible CGM; carbohydrate counting reviewed and pump automation settings titrated.\n</pre></div>"},"type":{"coding":[{"code":"34117-2","display":"History and physical note","system":"http://loinc.org"},{"code":"51847-2","display":"Evaluation + plan note","system":"http://loinc.org"}],"text":"Clinical note"},"meta":{"profile":["http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-documentreference"]}}
